trol) every\nsingle vertex of G. Also, for some graphs H it is clear that in this regime the lower\nbound has to be raised at least to δ(G) ≥r−1\nDate: August 12, 2008.\nThe ﬁrst and third author were partially supported by DFG grant TA 309/2-1. The second\nauthor was partially supported by DFG grant SCHA 1263/1-1.\n1--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPROOF OF THE BANDWIDTH CONJECTURE OF BOLLOB´AS (https://personal.lse.ac.uk/boettche/docs/BoeSchTa_BollobasKomlos.pdf)\nciteturn3search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; One way to rule out such expansion properties for H is to restrict the bandwidth ... paper we give a proof of this conjecture. ... The analogue of Theorem 1 for bipartite H was announced by Abbasi [1] in 1998,\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProof of the bandwidth conjecture of Bollobás and Komlós (https://eurekamag.com/research/086/890/086890697.php)\nciteturn3search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 18.8 years ago; Crawled: last month; # Proof of the bandwidth conjecture of Bollobás and Komlós ... 1982: On a conjecture of bollobás and bosák Journal of Graph Theory 6(2): 139-146\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPapers from 2026-08-22 - arXiv Combinatorics (https://www.arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/date/2026-08-22)\nciteturn3search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: today; # • INFO • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\nA bandwidth refinement of the Erdős distinct subset sums bound ... We prove the conjecture for $t$-designs, which are the $t$-wise balanced designs whose blocks all have the same size. Our theorem does not require simplicity, and we bound all parameters of the designs by explicit polynomials in $λ$.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMathematics: AI research tracker · AI Proof Watch (https://aiproofwatch.com/problems/mathematics)\ncit